 of paris state a transformation  more important than stopping climate  change  under brazil's president jeb bolsonaro  the cutting has increased  many here doubt his cop 26 commitments  will actually make much difference  trier nestles beneath the rainforest  it's the only town on the 163 that still  does  just 16 years ago though it was inside  the forest and all travelers passed  through it bringing trade  now it's off the main road the trees  have gone and nobody comes through  75 year old joao alves fedoza says the  road has been a disaster for their  economy and the environment  foreign  the traffic on the 163 never ever stops  occasionally it branches off to the  tributaries of the amazon  rivers that are the lifeblood of the  rainforest replaced now by tarmac and  mud  a unique vital part of the world's  environment  cleared out by humans  where even the living trees now stand  alone
 

